WEBVTT

00:15.100 --> 00:21.910
Kokoro no mori no naka kimi ni deau koto

00:15.100 --> 00:21.910
I was always dreaming of meeting you

00:16.100 --> 00:22.150
<b>Zettai Shonen</b>

00:21.910 --> 00:26.980
Itsumo yume mitetan da

00:21.910 --> 00:26.980
within my heart’s forest.

00:26.980 --> 00:33.120
Hikari no silhouette sono saki wo mezashite

00:26.980 --> 00:33.120
The silhouette of light guides the way.

00:33.120 --> 00:38.750
Itsuka ai ni furete mitai

00:33.120 --> 00:38.750
One day, I’d like to try and experience love.

00:38.750 --> 00:44.460
Kimochi to kotoba niji to mizutamari

00:38.750 --> 00:44.460
My feelings and words can be like rainbows and puddles.

00:44.460 --> 00:51.870
Omoiau yasashisa ga michibiku ashita he to

00:44.460 --> 00:51.870
The kindness we share will guide us into tomorrow.

00:51.870 --> 00:57.370
Kimi ga iru dake de tsuyoku nareru kara

00:51.870 --> 00:57.370
With only you here, I can become stronger.

00:57.370 --> 01:03.670
Sora takaku negai wo kanadeyou

00:57.370 --> 01:03.670
My wish will be granted in the heights of the sky.

01:03.670 --> 01:09.050
Nanika taisetsu ka wo miushinawanu you ni

01:03.670 --> 01:09.050
You won’t lose sight of something precious to you,

01:09.050 --> 01:18.320
Kitto motto kagayaku kara

01:09.050 --> 01:18.320
because I’m sure it’ll shine even brighter.

01:18.320 --> 01:23.770
Kimi ga iru dake de tsuyoku nareru no sa

01:18.320 --> 01:23.770
With only you here, I can become stronger.

01:23.770 --> 01:30.130
Ima dekiru koto kara hajimeyou

01:23.770 --> 01:30.130
Let’s start with what we can do right now.

01:30.130 --> 01:35.510
Mawarimichi demo ii jibun wo shinjite

01:30.130 --> 01:35.510
I don’t mind if we take a detour, 
as long as you believe in yourself.

01:35.510 --> 01:44.620
Kitto motto sono saki he to

01:35.510 --> 01:44.620
By doing that, I’m sure we can go even further.

02:13.780 --> 02:14.980
<b>I was...?</b>

02:28.930 --> 02:35.900
<b>The World’s Membrane Grows Thinner</b>

02:37.710 --> 02:41.240
<b>That’s the fire department’s job.</b>

02:41.240 --> 02:43.640
<b>It’d be another story if we were in a drought, but...</b>

02:43.650 --> 02:46.050
<b>...what’s so bad about water appearing?</b>

02:54.990 --> 02:57.490
<b>The water temperature in the
rice paddies is dropping?</b>

02:57.490 --> 02:59.490
<b>It’s dropped that much?</b>

03:03.530 --> 03:07.230
<b>Moron! Say that after you’ve actually
measured the water temperature!</b>

03:09.640 --> 03:10.570
<b>What’s wrong?</b>

03:11.210 --> 03:14.980
<b>Apparently, an artesian well’s popped
up near the recharge basin.</b>

03:14.980 --> 03:16.540
<b>An artesian well?</b>

03:17.110 --> 03:19.450
<b>A place where spring water comes out of the ground.</b>

03:19.450 --> 03:21.580
<b>There used to be lots of springs in the valley...</b>

03:21.580 --> 03:25.020
<b>...before an earthquake created a fault.</b>

03:25.020 --> 03:28.820
<b>And it looks like one of those
springs came back to life.</b>

03:30.690 --> 03:32.490
<b>A spring, huh?</b>

03:35.330 --> 03:38.970
<b>I wonder if there was one up the
Nakizawagawa River, too?</b>

03:40.000 --> 03:43.900
<b>You know how they’ve been talking about
a lot of fireflies being up there, right?</b>

03:43.910 --> 03:46.210
<b>And there has to be clean water for fireflies, right?</b>

03:48.040 --> 03:49.180
<b>I dunno.</b>

04:17.270 --> 04:20.270
<b>Aizawa Junko</b>

04:22.110 --> 04:23.180
<b>Hello?</b>

04:23.180 --> 04:24.650
<b>Ah, Ayumu?</b>

04:24.650 --> 04:26.750
<b>I sent you that picture. 
Did you see it?</b>

04:26.750 --> 04:27.250
<b>Yeah.</b>

04:27.250 --> 04:30.720
<b>Ayumu, are you really all right?</b>

04:30.720 --> 04:32.090
<b>Huh? What do you mean?</b>

04:32.090 --> 04:34.420
<b>What do I mean?</b>

04:34.420 --> 04:38.660
<b>You said you’d call me again yesterday,
so I waited, but you never did.</b>

04:38.660 --> 04:42.100
<b>And when I sent you the picture asking how you
were doing, you didn’t reply to that, either.</b>

04:42.100 --> 04:45.360
<b>Sorry... I’ve been sort of busy with my own things...</b>

04:46.000 --> 04:47.500
<b>Oh, that’s right.</b>

04:47.500 --> 04:49.240
<b>I heard from that man.</b>

04:49.240 --> 04:52.410
<b>You’ve made some friends,
and you’re always out of the house.</b>

04:52.410 --> 04:55.410
<b>That’s great. I’m happy for you.</b>

04:55.410 --> 04:56.680
<b>What kind of people are they?</b>

04:56.680 --> 04:58.110
<b>What do you mean?</b>

04:58.110 --> 05:00.210
<b>It couldn’t be that... 
you have a girlfriend?</b>

05:00.220 --> 05:00.980
<b>No.</b>

05:00.980 --> 05:05.520
<b>At any rate, it looks like having you go there
over summer vacation was a good idea.</b>

05:05.520 --> 05:07.720
<b>People might really be affected by their environment.</b>

05:07.720 --> 05:10.830
<b>I guess I was ready to accept that,
sending you there for a week...</b>

05:13.330 --> 05:14.730
<b>Hello?</b>

05:15.960 --> 05:17.940
<b><b>Out of Area</b></b>

05:21.900 --> 05:23.540
<b>Out of Area</b>

05:38.950 --> 05:42.620
<b>Please read the warning labels,
and follow correct usage practices.</b>

05:42.590 --> 05:46.060
<b></b>Because Love Exists,
It Conquers Everything

05:42.590 --> 05:46.060
<b></b>Coming up after this

05:43.290 --> 05:47.190
<b>“Because Love Exists, It Conquers Everything” coming up after this.</b>

05:52.160 --> 05:54.100
<b></b>It Conquers Everything

05:52.160 --> 05:54.100
<b></b>Because Love Exists

06:05.450 --> 06:07.280
<b>Come on!</b>

06:10.220 --> 06:15.080
<b>What am I gonna do about my daily “Because Love Exists, It Conquers Everything”?!</b>

06:15.090 --> 06:19.060
<b>Nekogaji
Street</b>

06:21.530 --> 06:23.530
<b>So it finally broke down, huh?</b>

06:26.710 --> 06:27.300
<b>Hey.</b>

06:28.040 --> 06:30.040
<b>Don’t say “finally.”</b>

06:30.040 --> 06:33.110
<b>I’m sure it’d be easier if you just walked
it home to your house to fix it.</b>

06:34.480 --> 06:35.650
<b>Let’s see...</b>

06:35.650 --> 06:36.810
<b>Do you understand this kind of stuff?</b>

06:36.820 --> 06:38.520
<b>Nope, not at all.</b>

06:38.520 --> 06:41.720
<b>I don’t think I can do anything about the EFI.</b>

06:41.720 --> 06:43.520
<b>EFI?</b>

06:43.520 --> 06:46.160
<b>Electric Fuel Injection.</b>

06:46.160 --> 06:48.460
<b>The system’s controlling device for the electric fuel.</b>

06:50.260 --> 06:54.300
<b>I was hoping to do something about the
carburetor, since I can normally do that.</b>

06:55.670 --> 07:00.270
<b>But it was riding fine before...
and then it suddenly stopped.</b>

07:00.270 --> 07:02.340
<b>It didn’t show any signs before it happened, either.</b>

07:02.340 --> 07:03.870
<b>I just don’t get it.</b>

07:03.880 --> 07:05.510
<b>It’s like what happened to our TV...</b>

07:05.510 --> 07:06.740
<b>Your TV?</b>

07:06.750 --> 07:09.450
<b>It just suddenly stopped showing anything.</b>

07:09.450 --> 07:12.120
<b>It’s just old. Probably just died.</b>

07:12.120 --> 07:14.620
<b>We just bought it last year.</b>

07:14.620 --> 07:15.220
<b>Right?</b>

07:15.220 --> 07:16.890
<b>It’s not broken.</b>

07:16.890 --> 07:19.720
<b>Well with TVs, there’s also things with radio waves.</b>

07:22.690 --> 07:24.700
<b>Hey, don’t go doing that without asking...!</b>

07:25.500 --> 07:26.430
<b>See?</b>

07:26.430 --> 07:27.600
<b>It’s fixed.</b>

07:27.600 --> 07:29.200
<b>It wasn’t broken to begin with.</b>

07:29.200 --> 07:30.770
<b>Don’t say it’s fixed.</b>

07:30.770 --> 07:32.340
<b>But it was just...</b>

07:33.170 --> 07:34.910
<b>Probably a bit sleepy.</b>

07:34.910 --> 07:36.670
<b>As if I’d be sleeping while driving!</b>

07:36.680 --> 07:39.310
<b>Not you, Ryousuke. The machine.</b>

07:39.310 --> 07:42.480
<b>You know... machines don’t sleep.</b>

07:42.480 --> 07:44.780
<b>When a machine suddenly goes to “sleep,”
we call that “broken down.”</b>

07:44.780 --> 07:46.980
<b>I see. So you can say it that way, too?</b>

07:46.990 --> 07:47.550
<b>Yes.</b>

07:48.920 --> 07:52.520
<b>The conversations you two have are so weird...</b>

08:06.200 --> 08:07.570
<b>All right.</b>

08:18.850 --> 08:20.620
<b>Come on, look alive.</b>

08:21.450 --> 08:23.090
<b>But...</b>

08:23.090 --> 08:24.620
<b>No buts.</b>

08:24.620 --> 08:27.190
<b>After organizing this many receipts...</b>

08:27.190 --> 08:30.290
<b>...and adding them all up but not
having them total correctly...</b>

08:30.300 --> 08:32.100
<b>...it’s really draining.</b>

08:37.270 --> 08:38.840
<b>I’ll give you two hours.</b>

08:38.840 --> 08:41.070
<b>Go off somewhere and recharge.</b>

08:42.640 --> 08:43.570
<b>Really?!</b>

08:43.580 --> 08:45.040
<b>Yeah.</b>

08:45.040 --> 08:47.180
<b>You’ll be able to focus once you get back, right?</b>

08:47.180 --> 08:48.150
<b>Yes, sir!</b>

08:49.010 --> 08:50.450
<b>I’m off!</b>

09:37.000 --> 09:37.800
<b>Hey...!</b>

10:25.180 --> 10:26.340
<b>What was that...?</b>

10:46.500 --> 10:49.900
<b>Didn’t you come here to discuss something with me?</b>

10:58.140 --> 11:02.610
<b>In the past, the upper regions of
this mountain were off-limits.</b>

11:03.280 --> 11:05.820
<b>But now, anyone can just come
and go as they please.</b>

11:07.120 --> 11:08.790
<b>That which is sacred, 
that which is mundane...</b>

11:08.790 --> 11:11.290
<b>The normal and the abnormal...</b>

11:11.290 --> 11:16.490
<b>In the past, the boundaries between those sorts
of things were strictly protected all the time.</b>

11:16.500 --> 11:20.360
<b>Should I be staying away from the headwaters
of the Nakizawagawa River?</b>

11:20.370 --> 11:22.100
<b>I don’t know...</b>

11:22.100 --> 11:23.300
<b>What do you think?</b>

11:23.300 --> 11:24.800
<b>I don’t know...</b>

11:24.800 --> 11:26.200
<b>Think about it.</b>

11:27.310 --> 11:31.580
<b>Even if it were off limits,
I don’t know the reason why...</b>

11:31.580 --> 11:35.450
<b>Also, “the sacred and the mundane” and
“the normal and the abnormal...”</b>

11:35.450 --> 11:37.380
<b>...I really don’t know what you’re talking about.</b>

11:39.020 --> 11:43.050
<b>With people thinking that way nowadays,
the boundaries of things shake.</b>

11:43.060 --> 11:47.590
<b>And when that happens, 
the world’s membrane thins.</b>

11:47.590 --> 11:49.030
<b>And because it thins...</b>

11:49.030 --> 11:51.760
<b>...those beings which should exist in other domains...</b>

11:51.760 --> 11:55.270
<b>...show up in our world.</b>

11:55.270 --> 11:58.500
<b>At least, this is what I believe.</b>

11:58.500 --> 12:00.240
<b>Is that good?</b>

12:00.240 --> 12:02.040
<b>Or is it bad?</b>

12:02.040 --> 12:03.940
<b>It’s neither good nor bad.</b>

12:03.940 --> 12:06.010
<b>It simply is.</b>

12:07.080 --> 12:08.850
<b>You’re Kishiro-kun, right?</b>

12:08.850 --> 12:10.380
<b>It’s Aizawa.</b>

12:10.380 --> 12:13.220
<b>This place is kind of mysterious.</b>

12:13.220 --> 12:16.990
<b>It could just be that the membrane around
here was thin to begin with.</b>

12:16.990 --> 12:19.660
<b>You went beyond the membrane...</b>

12:19.660 --> 12:23.390
<b>...entered the other domain, and become
involved in something, didn’t you?</b>

12:25.160 --> 12:27.160
<b>Don’t run from it.</b>

12:27.170 --> 12:29.630
<b>Keep going and stay involved with it to the end.</b>

12:29.630 --> 12:31.700
<b>Do all you can possibly do.</b>

12:31.700 --> 12:34.470
<b>If you don’t want to look back with regrets, 
that’s what you should do.</b>

12:35.370 --> 12:38.440
<b>That’s probably all I can say right now.</b>

12:44.720 --> 12:46.880
<b><i>Stay involved with it...?</i></b>

12:46.890 --> 12:50.350
<b><i>Even if you say that, Wakkun’s gone...</i></b>

13:05.340 --> 13:06.940
<b>Here you are.</b>

13:07.840 --> 13:08.570
<b>Thanks.</b>

13:10.140 --> 13:11.780
<b>Did you walk here today?</b>

13:11.780 --> 13:14.650
<b>I have to walk Taruto anyway, and if I don’t exercise...</b>

13:15.250 --> 13:16.210
<b>That’s great.</b>

13:16.920 --> 13:18.550
<b>Thank you very much.</b>

13:24.790 --> 13:25.890
<b>Shall we go?</b>

13:36.440 --> 13:38.400
<b>Taku</b>

13:56.250 --> 13:56.950
<b>Hello?</b>

13:56.960 --> 14:00.660
<b>Ah, hello? Are you free right now?</b>

14:00.660 --> 14:01.490
<b>What is it?</b>

14:01.490 --> 14:02.760
<b>Ah...</b>

14:02.760 --> 14:05.830
<b>I just came down from the mountain,
so I thought I’d give you a call.</b>

14:10.640 --> 14:12.300
<b>Hello?</b>

14:12.300 --> 14:13.470
<b>Want to meet somewhere?</b>

14:14.170 --> 14:16.070
<b>But what about your studies?</b>

14:16.070 --> 14:18.280
<b>I’m fine. I was just relaxing a little, actually.</b>

14:18.280 --> 14:19.740
<b>Yeah!</b>

14:19.750 --> 14:21.250
<b>Head over to the park.</b>

14:21.250 --> 14:23.450
<b>Okay. I’ll be right there.</b>

14:23.450 --> 14:24.720
<b>Well, see you there.</b>

14:28.290 --> 14:29.150
<b>Let’s go to the park.</b>

14:33.390 --> 14:34.360
<b>Did you wait long?</b>

14:34.360 --> 14:35.760
<b>Not at all!</b>

14:37.330 --> 14:39.930
<b>Are you making progress in your studies?</b>

14:39.930 --> 14:42.070
<b>Well... little by little, I guess.</b>

14:42.070 --> 14:43.230
<b>I see.</b>

14:48.640 --> 14:52.310
<b>On my way home from cram school
yesterday, I ran into Miyama-san.</b>

14:52.310 --> 14:53.210
<b>You saw Miyama?</b>

14:57.650 --> 15:00.150
<b>Yeah... on the bus back.</b>

15:00.150 --> 15:03.090
<b>She said she was out buying stuff to make
her costume for the Cat Dance.</b>

15:03.090 --> 15:04.960
<b>That’s so funny, don’t you think?</b>

15:04.960 --> 15:06.020
<b>I see.</b>

15:06.690 --> 15:10.160
<b>Making costumes every year for it... 
it’s just so stupid!</b>

15:18.070 --> 15:19.440
<b>Umm...</b>

15:20.140 --> 15:22.070
<b>We’re...</b>

15:23.940 --> 15:26.080
<b>...going out, right?</b>

15:49.670 --> 15:50.870
<b>Bye.</b>

15:54.710 --> 15:56.110
<b>Why...?</b>

16:56.540 --> 16:57.200
<b>What?</b>

16:58.700 --> 17:00.240
<b>What is this?!</b>

17:25.800 --> 17:27.200
<b>That was...?</b>

17:57.460 --> 17:58.700
<b>My oh my...</b>

17:58.700 --> 18:00.530
<b>And I just changed them the other day, too...</b>

18:04.200 --> 18:07.670
<b></b>Because Love Exists,
It Conquers Everything

18:04.200 --> 18:07.670
<b></b>Coming up after this

18:05.140 --> 18:08.610
<b>“Because Love Exists, It Conquers
Everything” coming up after this.</b>

18:13.140 --> 18:15.040
<b></b>It Conquers Everything

18:13.140 --> 18:15.040
<b></b>Because Love Exists

18:21.490 --> 18:23.790
<b>Not again?!</b>

18:27.130 --> 18:29.590
<b>Come on, not again...</b>

18:52.180 --> 18:53.520
<b>Come on!</b>

18:53.520 --> 18:54.950
<b>What happens with Takeo and Chizuru?!</b>

18:54.950 --> 18:58.660
<b>What does fate have in store for Takeo and Chizuru?!</b>

19:05.730 --> 19:07.130
<b>Huh?</b>

19:20.950 --> 19:22.350
<b>Hang out with me for a bit.</b>

19:22.350 --> 19:23.110
<b>Why?</b>

19:23.120 --> 19:24.880
<b>It’s bothering me again.</b>

19:24.880 --> 19:28.320
<b>Were you about to go to the
upper part of the river again?</b>

19:32.920 --> 19:34.290
<b>Aizawa...</b>

19:35.990 --> 19:37.090
<b>I...</b>

19:38.100 --> 19:40.400
<b>I don’t know how to say this properly, but...</b>

19:40.400 --> 19:42.870
<b>...you think everything that happened
is your fault, don’t you?</b>

19:50.710 --> 19:53.310
<b>Hey, let’s at least go somewhere else, okay?</b>

20:02.250 --> 20:03.290
<b>So, spill it.</b>

20:06.430 --> 20:08.260
<b>Even if I told you, you wouldn’t believe me.</b>

20:08.260 --> 20:10.900
<b>I’ll decide that, okay?</b>

20:10.900 --> 20:14.130
<b>I’ll listen to your story, then decide
whether I believe it or not.</b>

20:14.130 --> 20:15.930
<b>So why not first try talking to me about it?</b>

20:21.540 --> 20:22.840
<b>Wakkun...</b>

20:22.840 --> 20:24.110
<b>Kappa?</b>

20:24.110 --> 20:26.210
<b>No. Wakkun.</b>

20:26.210 --> 20:29.850
<b>Ah... now that I think about it,
Miku mentioned that name before...</b>

20:29.850 --> 20:31.820
<b>And Duffuru or something, too...</b>

20:31.820 --> 20:33.520
<b>Dosshiru and Shisshin?</b>

20:33.520 --> 20:35.490
<b>Yeah, that was them.</b>

20:35.490 --> 20:38.190
<b>Now that you mention it, you were also there that time, weren’t you?</b>

20:41.830 --> 20:45.260
<b>Yeah. So why not just try telling me everything?</b>

21:07.020 --> 21:11.620
<b>In total, there are four different
kinds of relative adverbs.</b>

21:11.620 --> 21:14.260
<b>And depending on its antecedent,
one of them will be used.</b>

21:14.260 --> 21:16.990
<b>And what antecedents decide
which one will be used?</b>

21:14.980 --> 21:16.990
<b>Incoming</b>

21:14.980 --> 21:16.990
<b>Taku</b>

21:17.000 --> 21:21.170
<b>Well, for the first one, we actually covered
it recently in your textbook.</b>

21:21.170 --> 21:22.470
<b>It’s the one used to describe a place you’re...</b>

21:22.930 --> 21:24.170
<b>Come again?</b>

21:24.170 --> 21:27.840
<b>You couldn’t keep your promise with Wakkun,
so things turned out like this?</b>

21:28.810 --> 21:31.310
<b>Do you think that’s possible?</b>

21:31.310 --> 21:34.380
<b>Well, it does seem like Old Lady
Okaka is involved in this, too...</b>

21:34.380 --> 21:35.910
<b>Back to that again...?</b>

21:36.450 --> 21:39.580
<b>This Wakkun wore a poncho and rubber boots...</b>

21:39.580 --> 21:42.390
<b>...which is what you wore ten years ago?</b>

21:43.220 --> 21:44.260
<b>Huh?</b>

21:48.560 --> 21:50.330
<b>I see! I remember!</b>

21:51.800 --> 21:54.200
<b>That was you, Aizawa!</b>

21:54.200 --> 21:57.070
<b>We actually met ten years ago!</b>

21:58.440 --> 22:02.040
<b>You were trying to enter the Touya Forest.</b>

22:02.040 --> 22:03.740
<b>And that’s where I...</b>

22:16.150 --> 22:17.920
<b>Did you just remember?</b>

22:18.860 --> 22:20.260
<b>Somehow...</b>

22:20.260 --> 22:24.900
<b>Aizawa, why were you so intent
on going in back then?</b>

22:52.250 --> 22:59.820
Daremo shiranai kotoba de kimi he to

22:52.250 --> 22:59.820
On that nostalgic hill, I sang out to you

22:59.820 --> 23:06.530
Utaikaketa natsukashii oka de

22:59.820 --> 23:06.530
words that no one else knew.

23:09.530 --> 23:17.030
Tomare soyokaze kawaranu omoide

23:09.530 --> 23:17.030
The dying breeze and my unchanged memories

23:17.030 --> 23:23.710
Sotto misete ano koro no boku wa

23:17.030 --> 23:23.710
gently reveal to me what I was like back then.

23:23.710 --> 23:31.150
Aa yume wo aishite hitori ni natta

23:23.710 --> 23:31.150
Ah, I thought that being alone

23:31.150 --> 23:35.950
Sore de ii to omotta

23:31.150 --> 23:35.950
and cherishing my dream would be fine.

23:35.950 --> 23:44.630
Haruka na sora ni wa ima mo kimi ga iru darou

23:35.950 --> 23:44.630
I wonder if you’re still there right now in the distant sky?

23:44.630 --> 23:53.230
Yasashiku ikiru yo afureru namida koraeta

23:44.630 --> 23:53.230
Now I lead a simple life, having suppressed my overflowing tears.

23:53.230 --> 24:02.010
Mirai no melody ga shizuka ni yureru kisetsu

23:53.230 --> 24:02.010
The melody of the future is in the quietly stirring seasons.

24:02.010 --> 24:10.720
Aitai na itsu no hi ka... mattete

24:02.010 --> 24:10.720
I want to see you again, and I’m waiting for that day.

24:10.720 --> 24:19.260
Aitai ne boku wa mada humming boy

24:10.720 --> 24:19.260
I want to see you again, but I’m still a humming boy.

24:19.980 --> 24:22.840
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

24:20.450 --> 24:22.710
<b>I am still a cat with no name.</b>

24:22.880 --> 24:25.220
<b>Huh? But isn’t your name Old Lady Okaka?</b>

24:25.220 --> 24:28.250
<b>Old Lady Okaka? How did you
get that name, anyway?</b>

24:28.250 --> 24:30.150
<b>Now that I think of it, why did
that old man name you Roku?</b>

24:30.160 --> 24:31.890
<b>Why was I named Roku?</b>

24:31.890 --> 24:33.560
<b>Taruto-chan, you sure are asking some
philosophical questions today!</b>

24:33.560 --> 24:34.690
<b>What are you saying?</b>

24:34.690 --> 24:38.360
<b>Heigorou has the character Go (5) in his name, so 
he just added one and named you Roku (6), right?</b>

24:38.360 --> 24:41.970
<b>Nene-chan named me after a cute stuffed animal.</b>

24:41.970 --> 24:44.300
<b>What? How does Taruto associate to being cute?</b>

24:44.300 --> 24:46.040
<b>Cute = Taruto?</b>

24:46.040 --> 24:48.940
<b>That’s not it at all!
Taruto = tart cake, doesn’t it?</b>

24:48.940 --> 24:52.210
<b>No! Taruto = Cute!
I’m not some cake!</b>

24:52.210 --> 24:54.310
<b>Enough! Let’s end this unproductive talk!</b>

24:54.310 --> 24:57.820
<b>Next time: “The Night of the Third Promise.”</b>

24:55.010 --> 24:59.950
<b>The Night of the Third Promise</b>
